Building a Credit Score Model

_______________________________________________________________________________________________________
Predict: Will a customer default in the next 2 years?

Target variable:SeriousDlqin2yrs
1 → Customer defaulted ❌
0 → Customer did NOT default ✅

Each row = 1 customer

Some important variables:

RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines → credit usage %
age → age of customer
DebtRatio → debt vs income
MonthlyIncome
NumberOfTimes90DaysLate
NumberOfOpenCreditLines

👉 These are like financial behavior signals

_______________________________________________________________________________________________________
WHICH MODEL TO CHOOSE

🔹 1. Logistic Regression (Baseline)

👉 Simple + interpretable
👉 MUST include

🔹 2. Decision Tree

👉 Captures non-linearity
👉 Easy to explain

🔹 3. Random Forest ⭐

👉 Very strong
👉 Handles:

Non-linearity
interactions
noise
🔹 4. Gradient Boosting (XGBoost) 🔥

👉 BEST performance usually
👉 Industry standard

🔹 5. (Optional) KNN / SVM

👉 Good but less used in finance














2. Credit Risk Scorecard (VERY IMPORTANT for finance roles)

This is HUGE for your profile.

What to build:
Convert model → credit score (300–850 type)
Show:
Score ranges
Risk categories
Approval threshold
Example:
Score > 700 → Low risk
Score 600–700 → Medium
Score < 600 → High risk
Why this is powerful:
Used in real banks
Shows business understanding, not just ML

👉 Recruiter perception: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

🔥 3. SHAP Explainability (Top-tier upgrade)

SHAP values

What to show:
Which features drive default risk
Example:
High debt → increases risk
High income → decreases risk
Visuals:
SHAP summary plot
feature importance
Why:
Explainability is mandatory in finance
Shows advanced understanding

👉 Recruiter perception: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
6. Power BI Dashboard (VERY practical)

Power BI

What to show:
Customer risk segmentation
default rates
KPI dashboard
Why:
Non-technical stakeholders LOVE this
Matches real job requirements

👉 Recruiter perception: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

🔥 7. API Deployment (More advanced than Flask UI)

Instead of UI, build:

REST API
Input: customer data
Output: default probability

Tools:

Flask API / FastAPI

👉 Shows:

production readiness
backend skills